# Retries (pack 4): first drafts were reviewed at 128/96/64/48px.
FIT = " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: it drew parts of the creature (and its rubble, spray or petals) reaching to or past the edge of the disc. This time draw the creature markedly smaller and tighter: the ENTIRE figure, including every petal, horn, droplet, spray and rubble chunk, fits inside a circle of about two thirds of the disc radius around the disc centre, leaving a wide bare charcoal ring of base plate on every side."
retry('gigantic-sandworm-tunneler', 4, comp=COMP + FIT.replace('(and its rubble, spray or petals) reaching to or past the edge of the disc', '(the four petals and the rubble heap) past the edge of the disc, so the token could not be exported'),
      subject="A gigantic thick tunneling sandworm rearing up from the middle of the disc, drawn compact and smaller: a very thick segmented earth-brown and dusty umber body with fine ring ridges and paler tan underbelly bands coiling once around its own base in a low small heap of broken stone chunks kept close against the body, the front third reared up toward the viewer with its head split open into a wide four-petalled flower-like maw, each petal short and lined inside with glossy red-brown flesh and a few blunt pale teeth, a dark throat at the centre. Everything stays tightly clustered in the middle of the disc. No lightning, no glow.")
retry('walrog', 4, comp=COMP + FIT.replace('(and its rubble, spray or petals) reaching to or past the edge of the disc', 'its shoulders, arms, horns, whirlpool and water spray filling the whole disc and covering the base ring'),
      subject="A towering horned water demon rising from the middle of the disc, drawn upright, narrow, compact and smaller: a humanoid torso and arms hanging close at his sides sculpted entirely from churning translucent bright-cerulean water with white foam crests and swirling current lines, a hooded featureless head with two swept-back curling horns of clear aqua water that stay close to the head, two pale glowing eyes, the lower body dissolving into a tight spiralling whirlpool tail coiling in the middle of the disc, only a few droplets nearby. Glassy, watery and imposing, small on the disc, with plenty of bare disc around it.")
retry('ink-squid', 4, comp=COMP + " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: it was drawn too small and thin, filling only about half of the disc width. This time draw the squid larger and bolder: the whole animal, mantle tip to arm tips, spans about three quarters of the disc diameter along its long diagonal, with a thicker, fuller mantle and fuller arms, still entirely inside the inner four-fifths of the disc radius.",
      subject="A bold ink squid seen from a steep overhead three-quarter angle, drawn large: a thick pointed torpedo-shaped lavender-grey mantle with a pair of broad triangular pale fins at its tip and darker violet speckles along the back, a large golden eye, and eight tapering arms, fuller and shorter than before, fanning out and back in a streamlined spread, two of them longer feeding tentacles with paddle tips, dark violet ink-stained ends. Streamlined, chunky enough to read at small size, complete.")
